---
import Base from "@/layouts/Base.astro";
import Bar from "@/components/Bar.astro";
import { ARMS, CATEGORIES, deskTasks, buildTasks, summary, attempts, matrix, fmt, REPO } from "@/lib/data";
const desk = deskTasks(), build = buildTasks(), sums = summary(), led = attempts(), m = matrix();
const byArm = Object.fromEntries(sums.map((s) => [s.harness, s]));
const noneTasks = desk.filter((t) => ARMS.every((a) => m[t.id][a.id].every((r) => !r.passed)));
const allTasks = desk.filter((t) => ARMS.every((a) => m[t.id][a.id].every((r) => r.passed)));
const desc = "Does the agent deliver business work an owner can actually use? 187 desk tasks and 20 app-build tasks with executable checks, 2,244 recorded attempts across four agent systems.";
---
<Base title="Business Harness Bench" description={desc} path="/">
  <p class="kicker">A benchmark for agents that do business work</p>
  <h1>Does the agent deliver work an owner can actually use?</h1>
  <p class="lede">Business Harness Bench scores the handoff, not the conversation: reconciled files, correct imports, source-grounded memos, and applications whose permissions and records hold up under use and change. Every task ships with its inputs, an owner's ask, executable checks, a generator, and a reference solution.</p>
  <div class="actions">
    <a class="btn primary" href="/results">See the results</a>
    <a class="btn" href="/tasks">Browse the tasks</a>
    <a class="btn" href={REPO} rel="noopener">Run it yourself</a>
  </div>

  <div class="grid c4" style="margin-top:40px">
    <div class="stat"><div class="num">{desk.length}</div><div class="lbl">desk tasks, seven categories, each with a reference solution</div></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="num">{build.length}</div><div class="lbl">app-build tasks, each with seed data, an acceptance checklist, and three change requests</div></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="num">{fmt.int(led.length)}</div><div class="lbl">recorded attempts in release full-1: 187 tasks × 3 repetitions × 4 systems</div></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="num">{ARMS.length}</div><div class="lbl">configured systems scored end to end: harness, model, tools, and substrate</div></div>
  </div>

  <h2>Desk track, release full-1</h2>
  <p class="muted">Attempt pass rate over all 561 scheduled attempts per system. Failures, timeouts, and grader errors stay in the denominator. Cells use different models, so this compares configured systems, not harnesses in isolation.</p>
  <div class="tbl-wrap"><table class="tbl">
    <thead><tr><th>System</th><th style="width:40%">Pass rate</th><th class="n">Passed / 561</th><th class="n">All 3 of 3 / 187</th><th class="n">Timed out</th><th class="n">Mean cost</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {ARMS.map((a) => { const s = byArm[a.id]; return (
        <tr>
          <td><span class="sys"><i class={`swatch s-${a.slot}`}></i><a href={`/results#${a.id}`}>{a.system}</a></span></td>
          <td><Bar value={s.pass_rate} series={a.slot} /></td>
          <td class="n">{s.passed}</td>
          <td class="n">{s.all_three_pass}</td>
          <td class="n">{s.timed_out}</td>
          <td class="n">{fmt.usd(s.estimated_cost_mean_usd)}</td>
        </tr>); })}
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p class="muted">{noneTasks.length} tasks were passed by no system in any repetition; {allTasks.length} were passed by every system every time. The full per-task matrix, category splits, execution accounting, and cost tables are on the <a href="/results">results page</a>.</p>

  <div class="callout warn">
    <p><strong>Read before comparing.</strong> These are recorded campaign scores, not a rescored or independently certified leaderboard. The three Proto cells ran flash-tier models and terminated abnormally in a material share of attempts, which is a budget and elicitation effect as much as a capability one. ERP.AI, which publishes this benchmark, also builds Proto. Details and every known gap are in the <a href="/audit">self-audit</a>.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Two handoffs, one principle</h2>
  <div class="grid c2">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Desk track: a folder and a short ask</h3>
      <p>The agent receives business-shaped exports, spreadsheets, PDFs, and an email or two, then must leave the requested deliverables. Inputs are messy on purpose: merged headers, currency strings, mixed dates, a requirement buried in a thread. Where the files cannot support an answer, the correct deliverable says so.</p>
      <table class="tbl" style="margin-bottom:0">
        <tbody>{CATEGORIES.map((c) => <tr><td><a href={`/tasks#${c.id}`}>{c.label}</a></td><td class="n">{desk.filter((t) => t.category === c.id).length}</td><td class="muted">{c.deliverable}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Build track: an application, then three changes</h3>
      <p>The agent must hand over a working application a tester can reach and log into, import the seed data, enforce roles and row-level scope on the server, show a live dashboard, and survive a restart. Then it accommodates three change requests without losing earlier requirements.</p>
      <p>Twenty applications: CRM, inventory, field service, leave, purchase approvals, invoicing, memberships, events, assets, helpdesk, vendors, expenses, quotes, donors, appointments, property maintenance, recruiting, work orders, point of sale.</p>
      <p class="muted">No build campaign has completed its human acceptance pass. The task packs are released and validated; build scores are not published. <a href="/tasks#build">Browse the build tasks</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>How a task is scored</h2>
  <div class="grid c3">
    <div class="card"><h3>Executable checks, conjunctive</h3><p>A task passes only when every required check passes: exact identifier sets, keyed values, live spreadsheet formulas recalculated in LibreOffice, sentence-level text rules, and task-specific graders. A percentage of checks is not a pass.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Positive and negative controls</h3><p>Every task's reference solution passes its own checks and the untouched workspace fails them. Generators are deterministic, and a seed flag re-rolls names and amounts for a sealed variant.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Reliability beside accuracy</h3><p>Three repetitions per task. The site reports attempt-level pass rate and the share of tasks passed all three times, alongside wall time, token usage, and estimated model cost.</p></div>
  </div>
  <p style="margin-top:24px">The full specification is on the <a href="/paper">paper page</a>; the protocol and grader are summarised under <a href="/methods">methods</a>; the setup and run commands are under <a href="/reproduce">reproduce</a>.</p>
</Base>
